---
import BaseMinimal from "../../layouts/BaseMinimal.astro";
---

<BaseMinimal
  title="Terms of Service"
  description="Terms of service for the Dolmenwood Hex Map"
>
  <style is:inline>
    body {
      background: #d5e3cc;
      margin: 0;
      font:
        15px/1.6 system-ui,
        sans-serif;
      color: #4a3c2a;
    }

    main {
      max-width: 640px;
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding: 48px 24px;
    }

    h1 {
      font-size: 24px;
      color: #2c1e0e;
      margin: 0 0 8px;
    }

    .date {
      font-size: 12px;
      color: #5c4e3a;
      margin-bottom: 32px;
    }

    h2 {
      font-size: 17px;
      color: #2c1e0e;
      margin: 28px 0 8px;
    }

    p {
      margin: 0 0 12px;
    }

    a {
      color: #7a5232;
    }

    .back {
      margin-top: 40px;
      font-size: 13px;
    }

    .back a {
      color: #5c4e3a;
    }
  </style>
  <main>
    <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
    <p class="date">Last updated: February 22, 2026</p>

    <h2>The basics</h2>
    <p>
      This is a fan project. It is not affiliated with or endorsed by Necrotic
      Gnome or any game publisher. The Dolmenwood Hex Map is provided as-is,
      free of charge.
    </p>

    <h2>Accounts</h2>
    <p>
      You may optionally sign in with Discord or Google to sync your map data
      across devices. You are responsible for your account credentials. We
      reserve the right to terminate accounts that are abusive or violate these
      terms.
    </p>

    <h2>Your data</h2>
    <p>
      Any notes, hex exploration status, or preferences you save remain yours.
      We don't claim ownership of your content. See our
      <a href="./privacy/">privacy policy</a> for details on data storage and deletion.
    </p>

    <h2>No warranty</h2>
    <p>
      This site is provided "as is" without warranty of any kind. We don't
      guarantee uptime, data persistence, or that the map is free of errors. Use
      at your own risk.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      We may update these terms at any time. Continued use of the site
      constitutes acceptance of the updated terms.
    </p>

    <p class="back">
      <a href="./">&larr; Back to the map</a>
    </p>
  </main>
</BaseMinimal>
